  "limits": [
    "Micro-camouflage and fabric details are illustrated approximations. A few unchanged LEFT poses retain narrow skin bands at wrists; the two repaired contact6 poses are fully covered.",
    "Extra calibration figures and held trials are not additional costumes or playable roles.",
    "Source and pose-plan approval for compilation only. Actual game, installed routes and production are separate checks.",
    "Closest reference-based 2D drawing adaptation; pixel-identical retail assets, hidden details, model dimensions and animation timing are not certified.",
    "Original PNGs and the unchanged historical alpha>16 ownership threshold are preserved; faint-alpha diagnostics remain separate."
  ],
  "observations": [
    "The adult Captain avatar wears the official Survive Naked Snake Fatigues cosmetic; it is not Naked Snake as a merged character or Venom. Canonical camouflage, black under-sleeves, single knee pad and leg straps are checked against original reference.",
    "Final RIGHT6 sourcefdbebd has one knee pad on the rear leg alongside the two tan straps, front knee in uninterrupted camouflage and both black sleeves to glove wrists. Previously defective RIGHT6 trials remain held.",
    "LEFT6 is the accepted distinct native source280fc with covered wrists; the unwanted LEFT6 changes on later RIGHT correction pages remain held. Full source mapping has32 distinct roles,12 source-native crown/heel points and no joined mapped body or lost/foreign alpha>16 pixels.",
    "Supplementary body height comes from an actually drawn neutral on its own exact page. The corrected calibration context explicitly distinguishes LEFT280fc and RIGHTfdbebd; no source height is borrowed from another costume.",
    "All public provenance references retain original SHA and actual historical URL/corpus identifiers; no private file path is presented as a shipped game asset.",
    "Root attests the identified original-game appearance: MGS1 unmasked Mantis or the official Survive Captain cosmetic named by the existing label. canonicalAppearanceAttested=true means this source identity exists; it does not certify pixel, mesh, palette or timing identity.",
    "Only the two canonical provenance fields and the inventory field name changed. Every PNG, geometry, pose, anchor, calibration, plan and source URL is deepEqual to the source already physically reviewed. The drawing inventory is preserved exactly as nativeArtInventory; no metres or physical scale is invented."
  ],
